  "concept": "A priority of 0 makes a router ineligible for DR election in OSPF.",
  "mechanism": "In OSPF, router priority determines eligibility for DR (Designated Router) and BDR (Backup Designated Router) roles. A priority of 0 means the router is not considered a candidate for these roles. Higher priority values (1-255) make routers eligible, with the highest priority router becoming DR. If there is a tie, the router with the highest Router ID is selected. The election is non-preemptive, meaning a new higher-priority router does not replace the current DR automatically.",
  "evidence": "On an OSPF broadcast segment, an interface priority of 0 makes a router ineligible to become DR or BDR. Among eligible candidates, higher priority wins; Router ID breaks ties. Election is non-preemptive: a newly arriving higher-priority router does not automatically replace the current DR.",
